# Adding a battle music track

Battle BGM lives under `public/audio/` and is listed in `frontend/src/game_music/tracks.ts`.
Tracks play only during matches (from mulligan until a hero dies).

## Steps

1. Place the source file under `public/audio/<slug>_original.<ext>` (any ffmpeg-readable format).
2. Encode a web-ready MP3 beside it (96 kbps, 44.1 kHz stereo, no metadata/cover):

```bash
ffmpeg -y -i public/audio/<slug>_original.<ext> -vn -map_metadata -1 \
  -c:a libmp3lame -b:a 96k -ar 44100 -ac 2 \
  public/audio/<slug>.mp3
```

3. Delete the original (`public/audio/<slug>_original.<ext>`).
4. Append `"/audio/<slug>.mp3"` to the `GAME_MUSIC_TRACKS` array in
   [`frontend/src/game_music/tracks.ts`](frontend/src/game_music/tracks.ts).

The playlist is shuffled once per match; when a track ends, the next one crossfades in.
Playback respects `galaguerre:sound-enabled` (same toggle as Cuelume SFX).
